{
  "@context": [
    "https://schema.org",
    {
      "dyad": "urn:dyad:term:"
    }
  ],
  "@id": "urn:dyad:dmc:dyad-operator/next-best-disposition",
  "@type": [
    "DefinedTermSet",
    "dyad:DecisionCriterion"
  ],
  "identifier": "next-best-disposition",
  "name": "Next-best disposition",
  "description": "How the home presents the questions it owes the operator: rules filter, judgement orders. A question is eligible only when every predecessor on a gating edge is answered; each eligible question is then asked alone, in a batch of its kind, or later. It authorizes nothing: it orders and times questions, and every Y still binds only what its own question names (Rule-2).",
  "dyad:decides": "Of the questions asked and not answered, and those ready to ask, which may be presented now, and is each asked alone, with others of its kind, or later?",
  "dyad:inputs": [
    "the board store: every entry's question, phase and kind (dmc/disposition-request.jsonld), and the optional keys what, why, how, counter, reconcile, present and gates",
    "each question's unit, the chat it was asked in (#670), and the dyad units: the home always and every unit the preference paired-units names (Rule-16 Presence)",
    "the gating edges, from records alone: an entry's gates list (#<id>[:<kind>], recorded by the home or the operator, never inferred by code); the parent-Done gate (Rule-3 Ledger: a parent's Done is not asked while a child is not terminal, blocked, backlog or holding its own recorded done-Y); a plan's order: required step lines naming another row's question",
    "edges that never gate: a row's plain refs, which is untyped, and merges after, which orders landing and not asking",
    "criticality, the inputs code reads: irreversibility (a destructive host action, a release, a publish) and binding size (the PRs a done-Y merges plus the rows it accretes or retires); the inputs only judgement sees, recorded by the home as present: solo with a one-line reason: reaches the world, money or credentials, verification against an output, novelty (the first question of its record or one with no precedent), and coupling (a Y that would change another question queued)",
    "the questions outstanding: their kinds, and whether one of them is solo",
    "the tunables open-kinds-max and solo-binding-min",
    "the operator's attention order (dmc/attention-strategy.jsonld, #705) and the operator's weights nbd-criticality-weight and nbd-age-weight, read from the operator's attention store first, then the preferences, then this record",
    "each question's age: the days since it was asked, as the board records it",
    "the preference attention-mandate, and each done question's row: whether attention-mandate opened it (its first plan entry is the mandate preference's, naming attention-mandate) and every PR it merges is attention work (dmc/attention-work.jsonld)"
  ],
  "hasDefinedTerm": [
    {
      "@type": "DefinedTerm",
      "termCode": "elsewhere",
      "name": "elsewhere",
      "dyad:when": "the question was asked in another dyad unit's chat than the reader's",
      "dyad:then": "not presented here: not asked, batched, deferred or carded; counted in the closing line's Awaiting part as `in <unit>`, and answered in that unit's chat; a solo's question is not elsewhere and is presented through the home",
      "dyad:effect": "shapes"
    },
    {
      "@type": "DefinedTerm",
      "termCode": "gated",
      "name": "gated",
      "dyad:when": "a predecessor on a gating edge of the question is unanswered",
      "dyad:then": "held back, recorded on the board and never refused; counted as `gated <n>` in Coming, its predecessor named on its card; it becomes eligible when the predecessor is answered",
      "dyad:effect": "skips"
    },
    {
      "@type": "DefinedTerm",
      "termCode": "weekly",
      "name": "weekly",
      "dyad:when": "under attention-mandate: on, a done question of a row the mandate opened, every PR it merges attention work, and no destructive or release act in it",
      "dyad:then": "recorded and deferred to the next weekly review, where every such Done is asked as one batch; counted in Coming as `weekly <n>`, never as deferred",
      "dyad:effect": "shapes"
    },
    {
      "@type": "DefinedTerm",
      "termCode": "solo",
      "name": "solo",
      "dyad:when": "the question is eligible and is of kind destructive or release (the core floor, Rule-8 and Rule-11), or is a done whose binding size is at least solo-binding-min, or its entry carries present: solo",
      "dyad:then": "asked alone, nothing else asked until it is answered",
      "dyad:effect": "shapes"
    },
    {
      "@type": "DefinedTerm",
      "termCode": "batch",
      "name": "batch",
      "dyad:when": "the question is eligible, none of solo holds, and its kind is outstanding or adding it keeps the kinds outstanding within open-kinds-max",
      "dyad:then": "asked with the eligible questions of its kind, in Rule-3's batch form",
      "dyad:effect": "shapes"
    },
    {
      "@type": "DefinedTerm",
      "termCode": "defer",
      "name": "defer",
      "dyad:when": "the question is eligible and ready, and a solo question is outstanding, or asking it would make more kinds outstanding than open-kinds-max",
      "dyad:then": "kept in the pending queue, recorded and never refused; counted as `deferred <n>` in Coming; asked when the bound allows",
      "dyad:effect": "shapes"
    },
    {
      "@type": "DefinedTerm",
      "termCode": "re-present",
      "name": "re-present",
      "dyad:when": "an outstanding question whose matter moved",
      "dyad:then": "handed to dmc/re-present.jsonld, whose outcome this record consumes and does not restate",
      "dyad:effect": "shapes"
    },
    {
      "@type": "DefinedTerm",
      "termCode": "suspected-edge",
      "name": "suspected edge",
      "dyad:when": "judgement suspects a dependency no record holds",
      "dyad:then": "flagged on the card, never applied: the home records it in gates, or puts it to the operator",
      "dyad:effect": "asks"
    }
  ],
  "dyad:precedence": "Elsewhere first: a question held by another dyad unit is presented only there and counts toward no outcome here. Then gated: a question with an unanswered gating predecessor is held back whatever else holds. Then weekly: an attention Done waits for the weekly review. Then the core floor: destructive and release are solo whatever a setting or a present key says, and no setting makes them batch. Then solo, then defer, then batch. A solo outstanding counts as the only kind. Inside each outcome, and in choosing which ready question the bound on open kinds defers, the order is the weighted order (#706 PR 2, #709): first the operator's attention order (dmc:attention-strategy: what is owed, then the goal tier, then today's focus); then the score nbd-criticality-weight × criticality + nbd-age-weight × days since asked, highest first, criticality as code counts it (the binding size, one more for a question checked against an output, a done, and one more for an entry marked present: solo); then the time asked, oldest first; then the row id. The weights are the operator's, read from the operator's attention store first, then the preferences, then this record; no weight moves a question from one outcome to another, so the floor, gated and weekly stand whatever the weights. A re-present outcome is the re-present record's.",
  "dyad:default": "batch",
  "dyad:tunables": [
    {
      "dyad:preference": "open-kinds-max",
      "dyad:defaultValue": "2",
      "dyad:allowed": "a positive integer (kinds of question outstanding at once; a solo counts as the only one)",
      "dyad:readBy": "guards/agent/board.py"
    },
    {
      "dyad:preference": "solo-binding-min",
      "dyad:defaultValue": "3",
      "dyad:allowed": "a positive integer (the binding size, PRs merged plus rows accreted or retired, at which a done question is asked alone)",
      "dyad:readBy": "guards/agent/board.py"
    },
    {
      "dyad:preference": "nbd-criticality-weight",
      "dyad:defaultValue": "1.0",
      "dyad:allowed": "a number, 0 or more (the weight of a question's criticality in the order inside an outcome; 0 turns the term off)",
      "dyad:readBy": "scripts/strategy.py"
    },
    {
      "dyad:preference": "nbd-age-weight",
      "dyad:defaultValue": "0.5",
      "dyad:allowed": "a number, 0 or more (the weight of each day a question has waited since it was asked; 0 turns the term off)",
      "dyad:readBy": "scripts/strategy.py"
    }
  ],
  "dyad:judgedBy": {
    "dyad:kind": "mechanical",
    "dyad:implementation": "guards/agent/board.py"
  },
  "isPartOf": "urn:dyad:craft:dyad-operator",
  "dyad:home": "playbooks/d-work.md",
  "dyad:alsoIn": [
    "dmc/re-present.jsonld",
    "dmc/disposition-request.jsonld",
    "dmc/parent-askable.jsonld",
    "dmc/attention-work.jsonld"
  ],
  "dyad:owner": "Rule-3"
}
